- Velvet panels (rich colors) — luxe, good for formal rooms and light control; works nicely if you want a dramatic focal point.
- Sheer panels layered with heavier side panels — airy and elegant by day, privacy and insulation when closed; keeps the room light to show off the pendant.
- Roman shades in a textured fabric (silk dupioni or linen) — clean lines with a refined feel; good if you prefer less floor coverage.
- Motorized roller or blackout shades (hidden behind a valance or recessed into a pocket) — modern, high-end convenience and a minimal profile to let the pendant stand out.

Questions to narrow it down:
- Do you want maximum light vs. privacy/blackout?
- Preferred material/feel (light & airy, rich & heavy)?
- Color preference (neutral, bold)?
- Do you want motorization or thermal/blackout lining?
- Room ceiling height and window dimensions?

